# Caddy for Kassa: HTTPS in front of the application. install-services.ps1 fills in the site
# (CaddySite.template) and writes the result to C:\kassa\config\Caddyfile (keeping the
# file that was there as Caddyfile.<date>.bak). To change something later, edit that file and
# restart the service "KassaProxy".
{
	# The management endpoint of Caddy is not needed here, and anything on this machine could
	# reconfigure the proxy through it.
	admin off
}

# The sites of the other installations on this machine (the cash desks of other companies), one file each in the
# folder "sites" beside this file: install-services.ps1 -NoProxy -ProxyRoot of such an installation writes its file
# there. With no file there, Caddy says so in its log and serves the site below alone.
import sites/*.caddy

__OWN_SITE__
